From: hashtagbasit
Subject: drm/msm/a6xx: stop GPU wake-ups losing GMU replies

The screen froze for good after wake now and then: "Timeout waiting for
GMU OOB set GPU_SET" or a GX_BW vote "timed out waiting for response"
with the reply sitting in the queue, then a failed recovery. Three causes
on the same path:

- a6xx_hfi_irq() cleared every bit of GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO although it only
  handles CM3_FAULT. The HFI reply and OOB ack bits there are polled for
  by whoever sent the request, and when the handler ran in between, the
  answer was gone and the poll timed out. Clear only CM3_FAULT, as kgsl
  does.
- The interrupt mask resets to 0 with the GMU power domain and is only set
  again after HFI start, so every resume raised the HFI interrupt and a
  late delivery hit the first case. Mask everything before the GMU boots.
- After such a timeout the GMU and HFI paths wait for a pending fault
  devcoredump with no limit. The devcoredump needs gpu->lock, which
  recover_worker holds around these calls, so both waited for ever.
  Wait at most 2 s and report the timeout.

Found by gennro on the Odin 2 Portal (A740); the same code runs on every
Adreno 6xx/7xx we ship.

diff -ru a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -64,7 +64,13 @@
 	struct a6xx_gmu *gmu = data;
 	u32 status;
 
-	status = gmu_read(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO);
+	/*
+	 * CM3_FAULT is the only bit this interrupt is unmasked for. The HFI
+	 * reply and OOB ack bits in the same register are polled for under
+	 * gmu->lock; clearing them here throws the GMU's answer away.
+	 */
+	status = gmu_read(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO) &
+		 A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO_CM3_FAULT;
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_CLR, status);
 
 	if (status & A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_INFO_CM3_FAULT) {
@@ -439,7 +445,10 @@
 		 * pending faults from the GPU and we are taking a devcoredump.
 		 * Wait until the MMU is resumed and try again.
 		 */
-		wait_for_completion(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done);
+		/* Bounded: the devcoredump takes gpu->lock, which recovery holds here. */
+		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done,
+						 msecs_to_jiffies(2000)))
+			break;
 	} while (true);
 
 	if (ret)
@@ -1336,6 +1345,13 @@
 	/* Set the bus quota to a reasonable value for boot */
 	a6xx_gmu_set_initial_bw(gpu, gmu);
 
+	/*
+	 * The interrupt mask comes back as 0 with the GMU power domain, so
+	 * until it is set below every HFI reply raises the interrupt and can
+	 * reach a6xx_hfi_irq() after it is enabled. Mask it all for the boot.
+	 */
+	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_GMU2HOST_INTR_MASK, ~0);
+
 	/* Enable the GMU interrupt */
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_CLR, ~0);
 	gmu_write(gmu, REG_A6XX_GMU_AO_HOST_INTERRUPT_MASK, ~A6XX_GMU_IRQ_MASK);
diff -ru a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_hfi.c
@@ -129,7 +129,10 @@
 		 * pending faults from the GPU and we are taking a devcoredump.
 		 * Wait until the MMU is resumed and try again.
 		 */
-		wait_for_completion(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done);
+		/* Bounded: the devcoredump takes gpu->lock, which recovery holds here. */
+		if (!wait_for_completion_timeout(&a6xx_gpu->base.fault_coredump_done,
+						 msecs_to_jiffies(2000)))
+			break;
 	} while (true);
 
 	if (ret) {
